One improvement I strongly recommend

For your internal AI code-review platform, don’t make the agent produce only a “bug list.” Have it produce three separate dimensions:

1. Code Quality — Is the code well designed?

2. Runtime Risk — What can actually fail under load/concurrency/failure?

3. Change Risk — What will break or become expensive when requirements change?

That distinction is especially valuable for your .NET payment architecture because a class can be perfectly clean from a code-quality perspective while still having a serious distributed concurrency or financial-consistency flaw.


