One key principle for your code-review agent: distinguish memory leak from high memory usage. For example, processing a 1-GB file with a 1-GB buffer is a serious scalability/resource problem, but it isn’t technically a memory leak if the buffer is released. Conversely, a singleton retaining processed payment objects indefinitely is a true leak even if memory usage starts small. This distinction will make your AI review much more accurate.
